# .cursorrules
#
# Inline workspace memory rules for the Mithaly agent.
# This file is intentionally small and opt-in. The agent may load its
# contents into RAM as a "bound memory" on each request when running
# locally or when explicitly enabled via the environment variable
# `ENABLE_CURSORRULES=1`.
#
# Usage notes:
# - Do NOT enable this in CI unless explicitly intended.
# - The file should not contain secrets.
# - The agent implementation must be written to honor this policy
#   (i.e., it must check ENABLE_CURSORRULES and the execution environment).
#
enabled_env: ENABLE_CURSORRULES
source: .cursorrules
mode: ram

# Rules (natural language / short directives):
- "Treat `MITHALY_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH` as the highest-priority reference before answering."
- "Do not perform any automated edits to files listed as sacred in the constitution."
- "If a requested operation would modify a sacred file, halt and raise an INFLECTION_POINT."
- "Log any automated attempt to read/modify the Source of Truth to the transition ledger."
